# CHAIN-LINK corpus · AXIS = which RETURN-TYPE ladder arm publishes the outer
# link's type. CELL SAMPLED HERE: the bool-returning STRING predicates
# (`is_empty` / `contains` / `starts_with` / `ends_with`) as the OUTER link of
# a chain whose receiver is itself a method call.
#
# WHY THIS CELL EXISTS AS ITS OWN ROW. The sibling rows sample the SHAPE of the
# link between two method calls (EFieldAccess, EIndex, EPropagate, …). This one
# holds the shape fixed at the simplest possible spine -- `h.make().is_empty()`,
# two adjacent method calls -- and varies the OUTER METHOD instead. That axis
# was invisible until it was measured: `h.make().len()` compiled and
# `h.make().is_empty()` did not, one arm apart in the same ladder.
#
# The mechanism. `infer_expr_type` publishes a method call's resolved type on
# the UNIQUE `expr_link_types[span.end]` key, which the lowerer's
# `lookup_expr_gir_type` reads FIRST for every EMethodCall; without it the
# lowerer falls back to the CONTENDED `expr_types[span.start]` slot that every
# link of a spine shares, and mints the outer link's destination with its
# RECEIVER's type. That publish used to be written per-arm inside
# `infer_expr_type`'s EMethodCall case, and only 2 of its ~26 return sites did
# it -- so the tag-check arm (`is_some`/`is_none`/`is_ok`/`is_error`, sampled by
# chain_link_method) worked and this arm, three lines below it in the same
# ladder, CC-failed with
#   error: incompatible types when assigning to type 'Str' from type '_Bool'
# The two bool-returning arms are ONE class -- `bool` regardless of the receiver
# -- and both publish now.
#
# THE CLASS ENDS THERE, and that boundary was MEASURED, not guessed. Publishing
# at a single exit for the whole EMethodCall case was built and it regressed ten
# `self_host_runtime` rows: the ladder's other arms answer from the method NAME
# without checking the receiver (todo/t0712), and the lowerer reads
# `expr_link_types` FIRST -- so a published guess OVERRIDES a fallback that was
# getting it right. Publishable set = RESOLVED, never GUESSED. Both halves are
# pinned by `self_host_infer_bool_arms_publish_chain_link` (tests/lints.rs).
#
# Sibling cells: chain_link_set_predicate (the Set half of the SAME ladder arm),
# chain_link_binop (the same outer method reached through an infix left
# operand), chain_link_method (the tag-check arm that already published).
struct Holder:
    String s

equip Holder:
    String make(self):
        return self.s

void main():
    Holder h = Holder("abcd")
    Holder blank = Holder("")
    print(h.make().is_empty())
    print(blank.make().is_empty())
    print(h.make().contains("bc"))
    print(h.make().starts_with("ab"))
    print(h.make().ends_with("cd"))
    # A non-bool arm of the same ladder, to pin that the fix did not narrow it.
    print(h.make().len())
    print(h.make().to_upper())
